The number of unemployed people in France rose to 2.7 million people, France's national statistics office Insee revealed on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c03f6cde-923e-11f1-8c80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/jos-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c03f6cde-923e-11f1-8c80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/jos-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60479a44-9235-11f1-8dcb-ada1b72c7d88</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 09:48:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c03f6cde-923e-11f1-8c80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/jos-1.jpg">AP - Nicolas Garriga</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'People at war have come to help': Ukrainian firefighters battle French wildfire</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260807-people-at-war-have-come-to-help-ukrainian-firefighters-battle-french-wildfire</link><description>
A team of 70 firefighters from Ukraine is on deployment in southwest France, where wildfires have scorched 42,000 hectares in the worst blaze in decades. RFI met the Ukrainian rescuers helping to put out the last of the flames.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e305f8ce-904e-11f1-9907-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-2027.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e305f8ce-904e-11f1-9907-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-2027.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dcd68664-919b-11f1-820b-7f942ad1b252</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 06:09:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e305f8ce-904e-11f1-9907-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-2027.jpeg">© Pierre Olivier / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ceuta and Western Sahara at heart of US-Morocco rapprochement</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260806-ceuta-and-western-sahara-at-heart-of-united-states-morocco-rapprochement</link><description>
Since late July, the United States has been increasingly signalling a move to strengthen its ties with Morocco, both economically and diplomatically. In 2020, the US backed Morocco’s autonomy plan for Western Sahara in exchange for the country normalising relations with Israel. Now, Washington appears ready to support Morocco’s claims regarding the Spanish enclaves of Ceuta and Melilla. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/427a96a8-90e9-11f1-a773-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-05T135156Z-302699241-RC2NPMAFOLSZ-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/427a96a8-90e9-11f1-a773-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-05T135156Z-302699241-RC2NPMAFOLSZ-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ce5abc4-9181-11f1-91c0-09d83fba7db7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:22:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/427a96a8-90e9-11f1-a773-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-05T135156Z-302699241-RC2NPMAFOLSZ-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">REUTERS - Violeta Santos Moura</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Fifa executives rally behind Infantino despite commercial plan fiasco</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260806-fifa-executives-rally-behind-infantino-despite-commercial-plan-fiasco</link><description>
Gianni Infantino’s position as world football’s most powerful administrator appeared more secure on Thursday after senior Fifa executives backed him to remain president despite his failed attempt to overhaul the commercial operations behind competitions including the World Cup.
